@SameenAhnaf Did you open this playlist from the channel playlists tab? I tried it and could not reproduce this issue.

This PR does not touch any playlist extraction code, so that issue may also occur when opening a playlist manually.

A quick fix would be to clear the cache and reopen the playlist.

> The back button on the top-left of the screen should behave just like the phone back button. 

@Stypox There was a discussion around this, and I think it was Mauricio who mentioned that the Back arrow works differently from the Back button. The button goes back through the entire chain of opened pages, but the arrow goes "up one level".

If that behaviour is changed, it would become inconsistent with the Back arrow's behaviour in the rest of the app.

> now the recording of past livestream doesn't even show in feed page (used to be able to see them)

> I renamed settings keys containing "live" to now contain "livestream" for consistency. This will mean that for users upgrading from test APKs the setting will be disabled.

@braboobssiere As stated by stypox you need to enable it again from Settings→contents→fetch channel tabs

@Feuerswut What backup are you importing? Is it an export that was made by a version from roughly three weeks ago?
If this is the case, please note that those specific backups are incompatible with the current version because I removed the changed behaviour again and thus one internal value type is different.
If this is not the case, please send the backup via email to `team{at}newpipe.net` for further investigation.
